FINAL ANSWER
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VARIABLE = SES (socioeconomic status). It is the only candidate whose effect on BA degree
completion falls from +0.3511 (p=1e-08) with SES alone to -0.1720
(p=0.02114) once race and academic characteristics are jointly included --
a sign flip with ~149% attenuation of the original effect, i.e. the SES advantage in bachelor's
degree completion is statistically absorbed by measured academic skill and class rank.
